# Files that do NOT require the GPU test suites to run before merging.
# Uses .gitignore pattern syntax. A PR whose changed files are ALL matched here has its required
# gpu-tests/* status auto-marked successful by the "GPU Tests Gate" workflow
# (.github/workflows/gpu-tests-gate.yml).
#
# This file is evaluated from the BASE branch, so edits here only take effect after they merge.
# Keep entries conservative: anything that can affect runtime behavior or the unit suites should
# NOT be listed.

# Documentation
docs/
*.md
LICENSE
CHANGELOG.md

# Agent / assistant configuration and skills
.claude/
.agents/
skills/

# Dev tooling and repo meta
# .fork-base.json is metadata consumed by NeMo-RL, never by the code under test. It changes on a
# rebase — but a rebase PR also changes source files, which are not matched here, so the suite
# still runs.
.fork-base.json
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.testignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
ruff.toml
codecov.yml

# Workflows with no bearing on the GPU suite. Listed FILE BY FILE, deliberately:
# .github/ also holds gpu-tests.yml, gpu-tests-dispatch.yml, gpu-tests-gate.yml and
# k8s/pytest-multigpu-job.yaml, which define, dispatch and configure the suite itself.
# Ignoring the directory and negating those back out does NOT work — gitignore cannot re-include
# a path under an excluded directory — so a PR editing the test harness would skip the tests it
# just changed. Add individual files here, never .github/.
.github/workflows/pre-commit.yml
.github/workflows/fork-base.yml
.github/workflows/README.md
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/
.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md

# Local developer tooling. CI never invokes any of it: gpu-tests.yml drives the suites through
# kubectl against .github/k8s/pytest-multigpu-job.yaml and references no make target, no tools/
# script, and nothing under the top-level k8s/ (which holds the component: local-dev pod specs
# used by `make test-unit-remote` and `make image-build-remote`). The image CI runs is pulled by
# the :ci tag, which moves only on an explicit promotion — so even the image-build tooling cannot
# change a CI result by being edited.
#
# Listed FILE BY FILE for the same reason as the workflows above: `tools/` as a directory would
# silently exempt any future tool that DOES affect the suites, and gitignore cannot re-include a
# path underneath an excluded directory.
Makefile
tools/fork_base.py
tools/sync_upstream.sh
tools/build_image_on_flamingo.sh
tools/test_on_flamingo.sh
k8s/test-pod.yaml
k8s/build-image-pod.yaml

# Tests that FAR.AI CI does not run. The functional suites depend on NVIDIA's pre-populated
# /home/TestData volume, and the gb200 launch scripts target ARM64 hardware we do not have;
# neither is wired into any workflow here, so changing them cannot affect a CI result.
# Revisit both entries if the functional or GB200 suites are ever enabled.
tests/functional_tests/
